                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "076ea43c-1556-3bd5-8f7c-520dc37b325f",
                        "entry_id": "7d4adf31-ad6d-3158-83c4-35244bf75169",
                        "glosses": [
                            "On certain chess websites: a move set during the opponent's turn which is played automatically (if possible) after the opponent has made their move, done in order to save time in predictable positions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Internet"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4b7307e-2660-4b57-aa87-699f40c17ec6",
                                "sense_id": "076ea43c-1556-3bd5-8f7c-520dc37b325f",
                                "text": "Kasparov's loss to Caruana was a tragedy in a winning position. He wanted to trade queens by Qe4-c2, but a mouse slip landed the queen on d3. He tried to drag it to c2, which the computer registered as a premove that fatally lost a bishop. \"Computers hate me!\" said Kasparov, who famously lost to IBM Deep Blue in 1997."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b216f39-2115-437f-93b6-84bde220cf27",
                                "sense_id": "076ea43c-1556-3bd5-8f7c-520dc37b325f",
                                "text": "Bortnyk's lead was never really in doubt and he converted game after game with brisk speed as premoves flew across the board by both players. Nothing seemed to click for Robson as even critical premoves seemed all too often to be mistimed: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84f61a4f-41bf-42e6-86f3-b61421d45f56",
                                "sense_id": "076ea43c-1556-3bd5-8f7c-520dc37b325f",
                                "text": "Premove — In online chess games, setting a piece to move automatically after an opponent moves."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
